<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds closed lower on Wednesday, shaken by growing economic monetary union (EMU) worries and after a surprise interest rate rise by the Bank of England depressed European markets.</p>
<p>&quot;The market was largely driven by technical factors,&quot; said one dealer. December long term futures on Meff broke a number of support levels during the session. Traders see the next key support level at 106.60.</p>
<p>The UK's quarter point rate rise to six percent was the first in Europe after a series of cuts. &quot;That was worrying enough,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
</text>
